# Everything that must NOT reach a customer's server.
# The zip is unpacked verbatim into wp-content/plugins.

.git
.github
.gitignore
.sswi-release-notes.md
.gitattributes
.editorconfig
.distignore
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.wp-env.json
.ship
.idea
.DS_Store

# LOCAL ARTEFACTS — EVERYTHING .gitignore KEEPS OUT OF THE INDEX.
#
# build-dist.sh rsyncs the WORKING TREE, not the index, so .gitignore buys
# nothing here: a file git is told to ignore is still sitting on disk and still
# gets copied. The sibling of this list in tests/js/contract.test.js asserts the
# two files agree, because every one of these was found the same way — by a
# local build failing on something a normal day's work had left behind.
#
# The phpunit caches and the zips are matched by SHAPE rather than by name, for
# the same reason the playwright configs further down are: there are two cache
# files today, and naming them is how the third one ships.
#
# Those shapes are deliberately not quoted here. bin/mutation-check.js finds the
# line it edits by first occurrence, so a comment repeating a pattern verbatim
# mutates the comment and leaves the pattern armed — which is precisely how this
# block, on its first draft, silently disarmed the playwright mutation.
.env
dist
*.zip
.phpunit*.result.cache
mutation-junit.xml
mutation-check-php.txt
# bin/set-version.sh's atomic-rewrite scratch files. Its EXIT trap does not run
# on SIGKILL or a cancelled runner, and one surviving a killed release would go
# to a customer.
*.set-version.tmp

tests
bin
node_modules
package.json
package-lock.json
phpcs.xml.dist
phpstan.neon.dist
phpunit.xml.dist
phpunit-integration.xml.dist
# Glob, not the one filename: playwright.staging.config.js was added later
# and shipped, because the blocklist named a file rather than a shape.
playwright*.config.js
Taskfile.yml
composer.json
composer.lock

# Repository furniture and INTERNAL DOCUMENTATION. A staging dry-run showed all
# of this reaching the zip: CLAUDE.md and TESTING.md describe the architecture,
# the security invariants and the known gaps, and .claude/ is local agent
# configuration. None of it belongs on a customer's server.
.claude
.coderabbit.yml
renovate.json
README.md
CLAUDE.md
TESTING.md
